  "slug": "tally-ledger-pdf-date-range",
  "title": "Choosing the Right Date Range for a Tally Ledger PDF",
  "description": "Set statement dates for a month, a custom period or an invoice follow-up without misreading the opening position.",
  "category": "Ledgers and PDFs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Start with the purpose of the statement",
      "body": "For a monthly statement, use the first and last day of that month. For a custom request, confirm both dates with the person asking. A PDF sent to discuss one period should have that period clearly visible in the header."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check the start and end against TallyPrime",
      "body": "For illustration, a 1 to 30 June statement may open at a different balance than a 15 to 30 June statement. A transaction on 8 June is part of the former period's activity but precedes the latter period. Compare the resulting opening balances with TallyPrime."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Verify the exported file",
      "body": "Open the PDF and read the header and the closing balance for the selected period. If it shows a different range than you expected, export again with the intended dates. Name the file with the period so it is easy to identify when you share it."
    }
  ],
